    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40299" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quŏtĭens-cumquĕ</span></b> ,
		adv., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>how often soever</i>, <i>as often soever as</i>
			(class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quotienscumque dico, totiens mihi videor in
					judicium venire, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Clu. 18, 51</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 3, 34, 84</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rosc.
				Com. 6, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Eum. 5, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc facite quotienscumque bibetis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					1 Cor. 11, 25</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
